# Order import / Order Reconciliation — soft-retired (26 Aug 2026)

## Invariant

**Bank statement deposits (classified) are the revenue SSOT.** Homepage order gross must not post as synthetic P&L income alongside Stripe/bank CREDITS.

## Cash path

1. Customer pays on SELPIC (often Stripe/PayPal).
2. Platform fees; bank receives **net** payout (batched).
3. Accounting uploads bank PDF → CREDIT lines become income.

## Soft retire (implemented)

| Layer | Behaviour |
|-------|-----------|
| Settings UI | **Incoming Orders** and **Order Reconciliation** hidden; Bank Reconciliation only |
| `syncIncomingOrders` | No-op (`INCOMING_ORDERS_RETIRED`) |
| `POST` accounting `/api/orders/import` | 200 retired no-op (no pending save) |
| Storefront `POST /api/accounting/orders/import` | 200 retired no-op (no fetch to :3001) |
| `recordOrderToAccountingAsyncWithRetry` | No-op (approve never waits on accounting) |
| Admin Orders UI | Send-to-Accounting removed; short note only |
| IndexedDB `incomingOrders` | Store kept; no new writes from import path |
| SetupWizard | Copy says order import retired |

## Do not

- Hard-delete IndexedDB store or import route stubs yet (schema / bridge safety)
- Import sandbox modules into storefront
- Treat Approve-to-ledger + bank income as both active

## Existing `selpic_orders` rows

Rare. Soft retire prevents new ones. If present, recategorise/exclude from P&L manually or with a future filter.
